# D10(a) NEGATIVE (decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-06): a local `&`-bind must
# not dodge the rejection by hiding inside a match-EXPRESSION — an arm (or the
# `else`) that yields `&a` still binds a mutable borrow to a name (the check
# recurses through match-expression arms). Pre-D10 this typechecked and then
# died at link with a garbage monomorphization error (undefined reference).
# Expected: error[E_LocalBorrowBind] at the initializer.
void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[int] b = [4, 5]
    int n = 1
    auto r = match n:
        case 1:
            &a
        else:
            &b
    r.push(9)
    print(r.len())
